<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     THE PILE — 200 applicants arriving in an hour, drawn one by
     one. You are the coral one. This is the entire argument.
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="band pile-band">
  <div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="band-head rv">
      <span class="eyebrow">What actually decides it</span>
      <h2>The first hour is the <em>whole competition</em>.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        In a small market an internship collects hundreds of applications before
        lunch. Recruiters stop reading long before they stop receiving. Being
        qualified is not what separates you. <strong>Arrival time is.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="pile rv">
      <canvas id="pileCanvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
      <figcaption class="pile-legend">
        <span class="lg"><i class="lg-you"></i>You, at minute four</span>
        <span class="lg"><i class="lg-them"></i>Everyone who arrives after</span>
        <span class="lg-count tnum" id="pileCount">0</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
